---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import CtaBand from '../../components/CtaBand.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import { SITE, formatDate } from '../../lib/site';
import { isVisible, byShortName } from '../../lib/records';

// Publication gate: unpublished records never appear here (lib/records.ts).
const universities = (await getCollection('universities')).filter(isVisible).sort(byShortName);
const rows = universities.flatMap((u) => u.data.programmes.map((p) => ({ u, p })));
const money = (m: any) => `${m.amount.toLocaleString('en-GB')} ${m.currency} / ${m.per} (${m.academicYear})`;
---
<Base title="Medical college fees in Ukraine: tuition & cost of study" description="How Ukrainian medical universities publish tuition fees, what the cost of medical education includes, and how we verify a fee before listing it." suffix={false}>
  <div class="page-head"><div class="wrap"><span class="eyebrow">Tuition &amp; fees</span><h1>Medical university fees in Ukraine</h1><p>We publish a fee only when it comes from the university's official fee schedule, with the academic year, currency and the date we checked it.</p></div></div>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Tuition & fees' }]} />
  <section style="padding-top:1rem"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>How fees are published</h2>
      <p>Each university sets its own tuition fee per programme and academic year, with its own currency and payment basis. Fees can change between intakes. For that reason every fee on this site will carry the academic year it applies to and the date it was verified. Fees from different years or currencies are never combined into a single figure.</p>
      <h2>MBBS fees in Ukraine</h2>
      <p>Many applicants search for “MBBS fees in Ukraine”. Ukrainian universities do not award an MBBS; the equivalent programme is <a href="/courses/medicine/">Medicine</a>, and each university publishes its own duration and fee for it. The table below lists the medicine fee per university as soon as it has been verified from the official schedule.</p>
      <h2>Cost of medical education in Ukraine: what a total includes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>University charges</strong> — e.g. application or registration fees, invitation-letter processing, medical insurance arranged by the university. Listed per university where published.</li>
        <li><strong>Accommodation</strong> — university hostels or private rental; prices shown only where a current official source exists.</li>
        <li><strong>Living costs, visa fees, travel, document translation and legalisation</strong> — vary by person and country; we do not publish estimates we cannot source.</li>
        <li><strong>Our service fee</strong> — charged by Ukraine Medical Admissions, not the university, and stated in writing before you choose any paid service. No service fee is charged to start an application.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Any “total cost” we show in future will list its components, sources and dates. An estimate is never a guaranteed total.</p>
      <h2 id="reading-a-fee-schedule">How to read a Ukrainian university fee schedule</h2>
      <p>Official schedules are usually published as a table or a signed order on the university's own website, often in its international-students section. Before you compare two universities, check that each figure has the same five properties:</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>The academic year</strong> it applies to (for example 2026/27). A table from an earlier year is not the current fee.</li>
        <li><strong>The currency</strong> and the payment basis: which currency the fee is quoted in, which currency it is collected in, and at what exchange rate and on which day.</li>
        <li><strong>The period</strong>: per year, per semester or for the whole programme, and whether the amount changes between years of study.</li>
        <li><strong>The track</strong>: whether the fee is for the English-taught or the Ukrainian-taught stream, because a university may price them differently.</li>
        <li><strong>What is excluded</strong>: medical examination and insurance on arrival, invitation-letter or registration charges, hostel, and the fee for any preparatory course are usually separate lines or separate documents.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Every fee we publish will carry those five properties and a link to the official page, with the date we read it. Where a university's current schedule has not yet been read, the row below says “To be confirmed” rather than showing an estimate from a third-party website.</p>
      <h2 id="questions">Questions applicants ask about cost</h2>
      <details><summary>How much does it cost to study medicine in Ukraine?</summary><p>Only each university's official fee schedule can answer this for the current intake. We do not publish an estimate, an average or a figure copied from an agency website. As soon as a schedule has been read on the official page, the fee appears in the table below with its academic year, currency and payment basis, and on the university's profile.</p></details>
      <details><summary>What does the tuition fee not include?</summary><p>Typically: the preparatory course if you need one, hostel or private accommodation, medical insurance and the medical examination on arrival, visa and travel costs, translation and legalisation of your documents, and living costs. Each university lists its own additional charges; we show them on the profile only once read from the official page.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Can fees be paid in instalments?</summary><p>Some universities publish a payment schedule (for example per semester). We record the schedule exactly as published and never promise an arrangement the university has not published.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Do fees change after you enrol?</summary><p>Universities publish fees per academic year and may revise them for later years. A schedule that states year-by-year amounts is recorded as such; where it does not, the profile says so.</p></details>
      <h2 id="indian-students">Fees for Indian students</h2>
      <p>We are often asked whether Ukrainian universities charge Indian students a different fee. We will state that only from each university's official fee schedule: if a schedule prices by nationality, the profile will say so with the currency, academic year, payment schedule and source. Recognition of a Ukrainian medical degree in India is governed by the National Medical Commission's current regulations for foreign medical graduates — check the NMC's own published rules before you apply; we do not advise on them.</p>
    </div>

    <h2 style="margin-top:2rem" id="by-university">Medical college fees in Ukraine, by university</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap" role="region" aria-label="Fees by university" tabindex="0">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>University</th><th>Programme</th><th>Tuition fee</th><th>Status</th><th>Checked</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {rows.length === 0 && <tr><td colspan="5"><span class="badge badge-pending">No fee verified yet</span> No university's official fee schedule has been verified yet. Rows appear here as each university profile completes verification.</td></tr>}
          {rows.map(({ u, p }) => (
            <tr>
              <td><a href={`/universities/${u.data.slug}/#${p.id}`}>{u.data.shortName}</a></td>
              <td>{p.name}</td>
              <td>{p.tuition.value && p.tuition.status === 'verified' ? money(p.tuition.value) : <span class="badge badge-pending">To be confirmed</span>}</td>
              <td>{p.tuition.status === 'verified' ? <span class="badge badge-verified">Verified</span> : <span class="badge badge-pending">{p.tuition.status === 'unverified' ? 'Pending' : 'Not yet published'}</span>}</td>
              <td>{p.tuition.checked ? formatDate(p.tuition.checked) : '—'}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note">Fees shown as “to be confirmed” have not yet been verified from the university's official schedule and are deliberately withheld. The first universities' official schedules are queued for verification; each row will show its source and date as soon as it passes. {SITE.disclaimer}</p>
    <p class="prose">Not sure whether you meet the entry requirements or which documents you still need? <a href="/admissions/#readiness">See how the readiness check works</a>, then <a href="/apply/">start your candidate profile</a>. It is free and nothing is sent to a university.</p>
    <p class="prose">University profiles in the <a href="/universities/">directory</a> will show full programme details once verified. Meanwhile read the <a href="/admissions/">admissions guide</a>.</p>
  </div></section>
  <CtaBand title="Questions about cost?" text="Start your free candidate profile and ask us. We will tell you what we have been able to check, and nothing is sent to a university." />
</Base>
